===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*men- (think)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|musik}}, {{m|enm|musike}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|musik}}, {{m|fro|musike}}, {{der|en|fro|musique}}, and their source {{der|en|la|mūsica}}, from {{der|en|grc|μουσική}}, from {{der|en|grc|Μοῦσα||Muse}}, an Ancient Greek deity of the arts. Surface analysis {{suffix|en|muse|ic|t2=pertaining to}}. In this sense, displaced native {{cog|ang|drēam||music}}, whence {{w|Modern English}} {{m|en|dream}}.

